@title Restore steps
# Restore steps

1. **Stop the writers.** Pause the nightly import so nothing writes to the volume while the snapshot is chosen and mounted for the restore.
-- Confirm the import queue reads zero.
-- Note the time you paused it.
2. **Pick the snapshot.** List snapshots for the volume and choose the newest one before the corruption was first reported by the monitor.
3. **Mount and check.** Mount the snapshot read-only on a scratch host and compare the row counts of every large table against the last nightly report before you promote anything.

1. Open the console
2. Select the volume
3. Press restore
